<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The rename field's box — HomeScreen.qml:2516-2521: Theme.ground, radius _px(8), and a border
    that is Theme.line while it is idle and Theme.accent while it holds focus.

    ⚠️ One shape, not a state-list selector, and that is deliberate: AmScale.applyTo() scales the
    corner radius of a GradientDrawable it finds on a view, and a StateListDrawable full of nested
    shapes is not one — the radius would stay at its design size while the box around it came
    down, which is the same mistake that was drawing the pills' end caps through each other. The
    focused border is swapped in code instead (PcView.showRenameHostDialog), through AmScale, so
    every number here and there is the QML's own.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android" android:shape="rectangle">
    <corners android:radius="8dp" />
    <stroke android:width="1dp" android:color="@color/am_line" />
    <solid android:color="@color/am_ground" />
</shape>
